  "articleBody": "Turning a garage into a bedroom, family room, or home office is an exciting upgrade, but avoiding basic planning traps will keep your project compliant and comfortable year-round.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n1. Assuming the space is already habitable: Garages were originally designed for storage and vehicles. Framing, slab dampness, and roof structures must be assessed rather than assumed ready for everyday living.\n2. Ignoring moisture rising through the slab: Garage slabs usually lack underslab vapor barriers. Installing finished flooring directly onto bare concrete invites dampness and floor failure.\n3. Underestimating heating and insulation: Garages have minimal wall insulation and drafty door openings. Upgrading wall cavities, ceilings, and heating sources is essential for winter warmth.\n4. Overlooking fire safety and egress: Bedrooms and living spaces require compliant egress windows, smoke and carbon monoxide detectors, and fire separation standards.\n5. Forgetting required replacement parking: Some neighborhoods require designated off-street parking before allowing garage conversions.\n6. Adding a bathroom without checking drain grade: Connecting new drains requires adequate slope down to your primary sewer main.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nA hands-on general contractor ensures framing, insulation, drywall, and inspections are completed properly. Call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your garage conversion.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
